From 636546fa5a9da4e6846673d2adbee89d7fe5936d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brunduk <nikolai.viktorovich@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 22:38:56 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] 360 viewer: hand the clock back to the wall clock when the
 audio ends

With HELLO_XR_AUDIO=1 the audio thread is the master clock: it publishes
a position after every pa_simple_write. When the audio stream ended, or
ended before the video, nothing published or invalidated it, so
playbackTime froze at the last value: the end of the video stayed frozen
on screen, Finished() never became true and a playlist never advanced.

When no audio packet arrives for 250 ms, mark the audio clock invalid.
AcquireCurrentSlot() then continues from the last position on the wall
clock, and takes the audio clock back if packets resume.

Found by the 2026-10-12 code review (reverb-g2 docs/147, H06-1). Not yet
tried with a two-file playlist.

Signed-off-by: brunduk <nikolai.viktorovich@gmail.com>
---
 src/tests/hello_xr/video360.cpp | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/tests/hello_xr/video360.cpp b/src/tests/hello_xr/video360.cpp
index 3d76688..db22b03 100644
--- a/src/tests/hello_xr/video360.cpp
+++ b/src/tests/hello_xr/video360.cpp
@@ -773,8 +773,16 @@ struct Video360::Impl {
             QueuedAudioPacket item{nullptr, 0.0};
             {
                 std::unique_lock<std::mutex> lock(audioMutex);
-                audioPacketAvailable.wait(lock,
-                                          [this] { return quit.load() || audioResetPending || !audioQueue.empty(); });
+                // No packet for a while means the audio stream has ended (or ends before the
+                // video). Stop being the master clock then: the last clock written stays put,
+                // and video would freeze on it and a playlist would never advance. The video
+                // clock carries on from it on the wall clock until audio is back.
+                if (!audioPacketAvailable.wait_for(lock, std::chrono::milliseconds(250), [this] {
+                        return quit.load() || audioResetPending || !audioQueue.empty();
+                    })) {
+                    audioClockValid.store(false, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+                    continue;
+                }
                 if (quit.load() || audioResetPending) continue;
                 item = audioQueue.front();
                 audioQueue.pop_front();
-- 
